  "heat_muggy_west_evidence": "[MBG/属] Scorch and general foliage decline may occur if soils are allowed to dry out.\n[NC State/属] Most plants in this genus prefer relatively dry air, but hairy alumroot ( Heuchera villosa ) will thrive in heat and high humidity.\n[NC State/属] Insects, Diseases, and Other Plant Problems: There are few insect or disease problems, but leaf scorch can be a problem for plants grown in full sun during hot, dry conditions.\n[Walters/品種] May need protection from afternoon sun in regions with hot and humid summers.\n[RHS/品種] Aspect: East-facing or South-facing or North-facing or West-facing",
